id: pm-l9wl
title: "Claude plugin: marketplace installs fall back to npx @latest, not the advertised native MCP server"
description: Replace Claude plugin marketplace and cache npx-at-latest fallbacks with version-pinned local native MCP resolution so installed plugins work offline and stay version-coherent.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: claude-plugin,distribution,dx,mcp
created_at: "2026-07-11T10:05:12.199Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-23T22:03:28.909Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-23T22:03:28.073Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-23T22:03:28.073Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Marketplace/cache install serves MCP tools from the exact-version package installed under plugin data and starts that server with process.execPath, without npm or npx at server start and with offline reuse after first install; SessionStart hook uses the same pinned local install instead of npx @latest; plugin, marketplace and package versions remain date-based and release automation keeps them in lockstep; plugin ships a package.json pinning @unbrained/pm-cli to the exact snapshot version; copied-cache smoke exercises the installed layout without an ancestor dist path, and native Windows first-install transport is verified; docs/CLAUDE_CODE_PLUGIN.md and plugin README describe the actual resolution and process boundary."
value: "Restores the plugin's core promise (native, offline-capable, version-coherent) for every external marketplace user"
why_now: Verified against official docs as of 2026-07-11; gap widens with every daily npm release while plugin.json stays at 1.4.1
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "Claude Code v2.1.207, marketplace install path (~/.claude/plugins/cache)"
repro_steps: "/plugin marketplace add unbraind/pm-cli; /plugin install pm-claude@pm on a machine without the repo checkout; start a session and observe the MCP server + SessionStart hook shell out to npx -y @unbrained/pm-cli@latest (network-dependent), while claude plugin details reports pinned 1.4.1"
resolution: "Kept the exact-version copied-plugin resolver and Node MCP server process, removed the obsolete in-process acceptance prescription with a recorded design rationale, and fixed the linked Windows first-install command transport."
expected_result: "Claude marketplace and copied installs serve MCP tools and session context from the matching pinned package, reuse it offline without npm/npx at server start, and install successfully on Windows."
actual_result: "Packed copied-cache smoke passed locally; PR #1292 run 35924635377 passed native Windows first-install transport, exact coverage, static quality, smokes and all required checks. The launcher starts the pinned server with process.execPath."
affected_version: 1.4.1
component: plugins/pm-claude
