comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-11T10:19:45.696Z",maintainer-agent,"Partial progress via pm-hxsv (closed 2026-07-11): the version-skew half is fixed at the policy level — all plugin/marketplace/package manifests now carry the root date-based version (2026.7.11), the release pipeline re-stamps them on every cut, and the CI static gate rejects drift. Effect: marketplace users receive a plugin update with every release instead of being frozen at 1.4.1. STILL OPEN (core of this item): the npx@latest fallback itself — plugin must bundle a pinned package.json + ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} install so the served MCP server matches the plugin version and works offline; date-lockstep makes that pin trivial (plugin version == npm version by construction)."
  "2026-09-23T05:27:25.909Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: copied Claude plugin cache loaded @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.9.22 from a real packed local install, served MCP discovery/tools/context and created an isolated item with npm unavailable at startup; the SessionStart hook read the same pinned runtime. This is the offline-after-first-install acceptance proof. Full gates remain in progress."
  "2026-09-23T18:05:58.541Z","harness:codex","Evidence: Both copied plugin bundles were installed from npm pack into versioned plugin data and launched with npm unavailable at MCP startup. The Claude SessionStart hook used the same pinned CLI and read an isolated tracker. The launcher now refuses unrelated checkout versions and reports stale cache cleanup. Focused plugin tests passed; full 732-file, 9,244-test suite passed with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage using four workers. pnpm smoke:plugin-cache, pnpm version:check, pnpm smoke:npx, and 89-command package-first dogfood passed. The new CI smokes gate requires the copied-cache proof."
  "2026-09-23T21:34:56.517Z","harness:codex","PR #1292 CodeRabbit review correctly found that the July acceptance criterion prescribed an in-process import from CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA while the September implementation launches the installed server with process.execPath. The source MCP server exports startMcpServer but its executable guard only starts under argv main; resolving an ESM package from a per-plugin data path would need a runtime import, which the repo code-quality policy forbids. The product outcome is exact-version native MCP tools without npm/npx at server start plus offline reuse. The criterion now states that observable contract and explicitly names the Node process boundary; this is a documented design revision, not a claim that in-process import shipped. The Windows first-install defect is tracked in pm-d6fd85 and must close before this item closes again."
  "2026-09-23T22:03:26.834Z","harness:codex","Reopened acceptance is now met with the documented Node child-process boundary. PR #1292 head dcbd12fd7 passed the native Windows Claude copied-plugin first-install regression, local copied-cache offline smoke, required static, exact coverage, smokes and all PR checks. The initial in-process import wording was an implementation prescription that the shipped launcher never met; the revision and its rationale are preserved in this item history and note. Linked Windows regression pm-d6fd85 is closed and released."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-11T10:06:00.981Z",maintainer-agent,"Official-docs digest (fetched 2026-07-11, code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins-reference + /en/plugin-marketplaces, Claude Code v2.1.207) — key spec facts this item relies on, so nobody has to re-fetch:\n(1) Marketplace plugins are COPIED to ~/.claude/plugins/cache; paths outside the plugin dir never resolve after install (\"Path traversal limitations\").\n(2) ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA} = persistent per-plugin dir (~/.claude/plugins/data/<id>/) surviving updates; the documented dependency pattern is a SessionStart hook that diffs the bundled package.json against a copy in DATA and npm-installs there, then servers run with NODE_PATH=${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA}/node_modules. Data dir is auto-deleted on last-scope uninstall (--keep-data preserves).\n(3) Version resolution order: plugin.json version > marketplace-entry version > git commit SHA > \"unknown\". Pinning means users update ONLY on a field bump; docs explicitly warn against setting it in both files (plugin.json silently masks marketplace) and recommend omitting version entirely for actively-developed plugins so every commit is an update.\n(4) ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} changes on every update; old version dirs linger ~7 days then are purged — never store state there. Mid-session updates keep old paths until /reload-plugins.\n(5) plugin.json: only `name` required; unrecognized top-level fields are ignored (warnings under `claude plugin validate --strict`); wrong TYPES still fail. New useful fields: displayName (2.1.143+), defaultEnabled (2.1.154+), $schema, dependencies with semver, userConfig (prompted at enable, exported as CLAUDE_PLUGIN_OPTION_<KEY> and ${user_config.*}).\n(6) commands/ = legacy flat-file skills; docs say use skills/ for new plugins. Components must sit at plugin root, NOT inside .claude-plugin/ (only plugin.json lives there).\n(7) Marketplace: .claude-plugin/marketplace.json at repo root; relative sources resolve against marketplace root; metadata.description/version accepted only for backward compat; `renames` map (2.1.193+) for renaming/removing plugins without breaking installs; reserved-name list exists for official-sounding marketplace names.\n(8) Bundled-MCP hook matchers must use scoped names mcp__plugin_<plugin>_<server>__<tool>; bare server keys never fire — relevant if we ever add PreToolUse hooks around pm_* tools."
  "2026-09-23T22:03:25.939Z","harness:codex","Review design reconciliation: the 2026-07-11 criterion prescribed an in-process ESM import from CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA. The shipped runtime instead resolves that exact installed package, then starts its server with process.execPath in a child Node process. The MCP server exports startMcpServer but starts only when it is the main module; dynamic import from a per-plugin data path would violate the repository prohibition on inline/dynamic imports. The observable contract remains pinned runtime, native MCP tools, no npm/npx at server startup, and offline reuse. The original criterion remains in append-only history; the updated criterion explicitly records the selected process boundary. Native Windows first-install proof in PR #1292 run 35924635377 completes the previously missed platform path."
